---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <img class="hero-art" src="/images/black-hole-mobile.webp" alt="Amber accretion light around a black hole, rendered in ASCII" width="1200" height="1200" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="hero-shade"></div>
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN SOURCE / WEB + TERMINAL</p><h1>Light,<br /><em>bent.</em></h1><p class="lede">A black hole you can get lost in.<br />A renderer you can make your own.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/explore/">Enter the explorer <span>↗</span></a><a class="button" href="/docs/">Start building <span>→</span></a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-caption"><span>01 / EVENT HORIZON</span><span>LIGHT → LENSING → GLYPHS</span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="intro section"><p class="eyebrow">A SMALL UNIVERSE, EVERYWHERE.</p><div><h2>From a browser canvas<br />to your command line.</h2><p>Orbit the horizon. Strip the light down to characters. Take the same visual language into a React app, a Rust terminal, or your Ghostty background.</p></div></section>
  <section class="paths section" aria-label="Ways to use Blackhole">
    <a class="path" href="/explore/"><span class="eyebrow">01 / EXPLORE</span><h3>Change your perspective.</h3><p>Camera presets, raw light, ASCII, and a few well-chosen dials. Every setup has a link.</p><span class="path-link">Open the live renderer ↗</span></a>
    <a class="path" href="/docs/"><span class="eyebrow">02 / BUILD</span><h3>Bring your own canvas.</h3><p>A reusable renderer and a React component. The visuals belong in your project, too.</p><span class="path-link">Read the web guide →</span></a>
    <a class="path" href="/docs/terminal/"><span class="eyebrow">03 / TERMINAL</span><h3>Beyond the browser.</h3><p>Rust and Ratatui for the terminal. The same ray-traced ASCII scene in Ghostty.</p><span class="path-link">Find your integration →</span></a>
  </section>
  <section class="install section"><div><p class="eyebrow">START WITH ONE COMPONENT</p><h2>A little gravity<br />goes a long way.</h2></div><div><pre><code is:raw>import { BlackHole } from '@austindelic/blackhole/react';

&lt;div style={{ height: '100vh' }}&gt;
  &lt;BlackHole showControls={false} /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Installation, configuration, and source →</a></div></section>
</Layout>
